// "[subject] is [predicate]" ([CR#603.4]) — the SUBJECT-STATE shape a
// conditional static composes ("As long as enchanted creature is black, …",
// "As long as ~ is attacking, …"): `Matches(<subject>, <predicate>)`.
// `Param(0)` is the closed subject-reference vocabulary
// `crate::parsers::condition::SUBJECT_WORDS` accepts (`~`/"it" -> This,
// "enchanted creature"/"enchanted permanent" -> AttachHostOf(This)); `Param(1)`
// is a color, "legendary", a combat/tap-state word
// (attacking/blocking/tapped/untapped), or a full object-description noun
// phrase ("a Human", "a creature").
//
// Template: "${0} is ${1}" renders via a hand-written `Matches` arm
// (`crates/deckmaste_cards/src/render/condition.rs`'s `matches_phrase`) — the
// generic macro-template filler can't tell "is legendary" from "is a Human"
// apart from "is attacking", so this shape gets its own render arm on the
// CORE `Matches` variant rather than the template.
//
// Usage: SubjectIs(This, Attacking) / SubjectIs(AttachHostOf(This),
// ColorIs(Black)).
(
    name: "SubjectIs",
    template: "${0} is ${1}",
    kinds: [Condition],
    params: [Reference, Predicate],
    body: Matches(Param(0), Param(1)),
)
